{
  "paragraph": "Botswana faces a markedly deteriorated macroeconomic outlook following a persistent decline in natural diamond demand, which led to a sharp economic contraction in 2024 alongside widening fiscal and current account deficits. Buffeted by historical shocks from 2008, 2014, and 2020, rapid depletion of external reserves and fiscal buffers has placed the country at a critical juncture. The section recommends urgent action to arrest this deterioration and stabilize the macroeconomic outlook, specifically by advancing delayed fiscal consolidation and adopting reforms to foster economic diversification."
