{
  "paragraph": "Staff concludes that Botswana’s outlook is clouded by a diamond sector contraction, with inflation rising towards the end of 2025. Staff recommends adopting a three-pronged NDP strategy: near-term fiscal consolidation through tax base broadening, wage bill cuts, and SOE reforms; monetary tightening; and economic diversification. Authorities must also implement remaining FSAP recommendations to improve liquidity, tackle structural bottlenecks including SME finance and red tape, and fix IFMIS technical problems to enhance data quality. The next Article IV consultation is recommended on the standard 12-month cycle."
