{
  "paragraph": "Botswana's overall risk of sovereign stress is assessed as moderate, although debt does not stabilize under the baseline scenario, climbing from 33.1 percent of GDP in 2024 to 75.8 percent in 2034. The debt fanchart indicates high risk with a 99.9 percent probability of debt non-stabilization, while gross financing needs point to moderate risk with an index of 12.6. The report recommends implementing an ambitious reform agenda aimed at economic diversification to place public debt on a sustainable downward trajectory."
